WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: ar

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.280
This book is very old

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:05.600
by a traveler, in 1865

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.960
who traveled

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.600
around the Arabian Peninsula

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.960
This radio was made in the 1950s, 1953

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.160
If you come closer, you'll find all the radio stations

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.920
You can say it started

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.800
a long time ago

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.000
As a child

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:21.720
I liked the old vintage things I saw in movies

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.280
like typewriters

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.000
old cameras

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.520
Even you when watching a movie

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.280
about the 1940s

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.880
if you see one of these pieces, you'll feel a need to touch it

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.400
to feel it

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:35.800
In a part of my childhood

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:37.280
I was very interested in trading

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.840
When I was around 11 years old

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.480
 in the village where we used to live 

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.600
not literally, but we would go to it at Eid

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.800
We have this custom on specific days of Ramadan

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.600
similar to Gargeea'n, we call it Hwam.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.000
So

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:51.960
the candies I get

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.480
I would put aside what I don't like

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.080
and I would sell them

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.960
and I would feel good after it

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.200
since I am selling something desired by someone else

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.400
sometimes, I would even go out to the street and stop cars

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.240
and sell my sweets for those who want

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.880
I would double the price definitely

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:08.780
That was

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.160
 the beginning of my trade

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.960
By time, I grew up with the tendency of possessing antiques

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.360
Even when I visit people's homes

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.840
and notice some remarkable pieces, I  would ask them about 

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.960
I get interested, especially if they are inherited

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.240
Sometimes the same piece has some details like carved date

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.440
This is a gentleman's bowler hat

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.000
of

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.320
the late nineteenth century

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.760
1889

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.480
This is natural leather

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.880
 and the inside is of silk

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.080
 Some pieces

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.560
their stories will remain unknown

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.920
and will remain lost in time

00:02:55.960 --> 00:03:01.440
but it is enough for me to know it was owned by someone

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.800
This photo

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.160
was taken in 1985

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:09.320
in Rafha, near the Iraqi boarders

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:13.480
during the First Gulf War, or before that

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:14.800
I tried to find them on Twitter

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.000
I had a full name on the photo

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.720
I found someone with a similar name, and contacted him

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.080
he told me that the boy was his brother

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.640
so I will get in touch with the person in the photo

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.160
and send it to him

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.520
Nowadays, factories make

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.760
many copies of a piece

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:34.840
So, sometimes

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.600
these pieces lose its value

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.640
It made us lose

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.000
our appreciation of the piece

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.880
We start seeing it

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.000
like any consumed ordinary object

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.320
If it is broken,

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:53.200
we get rid of it

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.560
While in the past, they would get it repaired 

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.880
These old pieces

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.160
belonged to people before, but they gave them up

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:08.880
I feel that I don't have the right to keep those pieces

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.600
I am supposed to give them away

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:11.360
Some pieces

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:13.560
the piece itself becomes

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.880
I mean its value increases over time

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:17.880
not in price but in value

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.240
It increases because of the story behind it

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.680
Some pieces have lovely stories

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.520
One of the old doors I had

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:28.720
It is nearly 70 years old

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.360
I traveled to Az-Zulfi to buy it

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.840
It was owned by

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:34.720
a man who had his own old museum 

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.200
He had grown old and wanted to sell the door

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:39.680
so he told me the door's story

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.280
He said he bought this door from someone

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:43.800
from Asharqia

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.560
bought it with its padlock

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.800
Which means this door was locked all that time

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:52.200
and was never opened again

